{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1777472219,"nonce":"8mFpADuXQYUTdB3rpTWIoJSkiu4=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABA1q6FQ","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/107","origin":"github"},"title":"Reconcile gitcloud/jazzy with GitHub jazzy after #102 merge","message":"## Problem\n\nCannot fast-forward push `jazzy` to gitcloud after merging #102. Gitcloud has one trailing field commit `6c177fb \"Adding mavproxy param dump from before battery value corrections\"` that we already cherry-picked locally as `d01764b` (note the explicit `(cherry picked from commit 6c177fb...)` trailer in `d01764b`'s message).\n\nContent is fully in sync — same author, same date, same 938-line `.parm` file. Only the SHAs differ, which trips the non-fast-forward check on `git push gitcloud jazzy`.\n\n## Symptom\n\n```\n$ .agent/scripts/push_remote.py --remote gitcloud\n...\nunh_echoboats_project11\n  error: push jazzy failed: To gitcloud:field/unh_echoboats_project11.git\n   ! [rejected]        jazzy -\u003e jazzy (non-fast-forward)\n```\n\n31 of 32 workspace repos pushed cleanly; this is the lone holdout.\n\n## Fix\n\nSame precedent as `35759f6 \"Merge gitcloud/jazzy: field agent commits from 2026-04-27 deployment\"` (which landed inside PR #94's feature branch): open a worktree, run `git merge --no-ff gitcloud/jazzy` to record an empty merge marker tying the two histories together, PR-merge to `jazzy`, then `push_remote.py --remote gitcloud` fast-forwards cleanly.\n\nNo content change — the merge resolves trivially because gitcloud's tree is already a strict subset of ours.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nThis is a plumbing / history reconciliation only. No file changes. The actual code state on `jazzy` is already correct after #102.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}